    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0356" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1995</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Financial Adviser to the Republic of
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bussell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American Minister
                        in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>)<anchor n="16" xml:id="d192-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise that on February
                    14, 1928, I received a Commission, dated February 13, 1928, as Acting Financial
                    Adviser from His Excellency the President of Liberia, and on February 14th I
                    assumed the duties of that position.</p>
                <p>2. I wish to take this opportunity of expressing my appreciation of the courteous
                    cooperation received by me from the American Legation in the past and venture to
                    hope that the same will continue in the future.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>C. T. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bussell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d192-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d192-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted by the Minister in Liberia in his despatch No. 33, Feb. 15,
                    1928; received March 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
